  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "DOReaderCache breaks JEE compliance by implementing an unmanaged thread, which is restricted in EJB spec:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "marks": [
            {
             "attrs": {
              "href": "http://stackoverflow.com/questions/533783/why-spawning-threads-in-j2ee-container-is-discouraged"
             },
             "type": "link"
            }
           ],
           "text": "http://stackoverflow.com/questions/533783/why-spawning-threads-in-j2ee-container-is-discouraged",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "marks": [
            {
             "attrs": {
              "href": "http://java.sun.com/blueprints/guidelines/designing_enterprise_applications/ejb_tier/qanda/restrictions.html"
             },
             "type": "link"
            }
           ],
           "text": "http://java.sun.com/blueprints/guidelines/designing_enterprise_applications/ejb_tier/qanda/restrictions.html",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Furthermore the usage of List is quite peculiar, where type and semantics are dependent on the index of the object in the list. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
