  "description": "<p>DOReaderCache breaks JEE compliance by implementing an unmanaged thread, which is restricted in EJB spec:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/533783/why-spawning-threads-in-j2ee-container-is-discouraged\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/533783/why-spawning-threads-in-j2ee-container-is-discouraged</a></li>\n\t<li><a href=\"http://java.sun.com/blueprints/guidelines/designing_enterprise_applications/ejb_tier/qanda/restrictions.html\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://java.sun.com/blueprints/guidelines/designing_enterprise_applications/ejb_tier/qanda/restrictions.html</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>Furthermore the usage of List is quite peculiar, where type and semantics are dependent on the index of the object in the list. </p>",
